The makers of Jailer 2 shot and completed the film's promotional teaser by 6 December 2024 at EVP Film City in Chennai, which was officially released on 14 January 2025, coinciding with Pongal.
Cinematographer Vijay Kartik Kannan returned for the sequel after working on the predecessor. Nelson further renewed his norm technicians—music composer Anirudh Ravichander, editor R. Nirmal, production designer D. R. K. Kiran—who also worked on the predecessor;
By late December 2024, Nelson began location scouting for the film. Initially, the film was set to begin production in late 2024 in order to be released during 2025, as it would mark Rajinikanth's 50th year in the film industry. However, the plans were rescinded owing to pre-production delays, resulting in the film's eventual commencement being pushed to March 2025.

Series 3 debuted 17 October 2014.
